que), based only on the movement data.\n2. One positive observation - something Player 1 did well during this moment.\n3. Exactly three alternative tactical moves Player 1 could have made instead, written in simple, beginner-friendly language a new player could understand.\n\nAlways refer to the players as \"Player 1\" and \"Player 2\" - never use any other name or label for them. Do not include any section, heading, or commentary other than the three items above.\n\nRespond with ONLY this JSON object, no other text:\n{\n  \"identified_move\": \"<short phrase>\",\n  \"positive_observation\": \"<one sentence>\",\n  \"alternative_moves\": [\"<move 1>\", \"<move 2>\", \"<move 3>\"]\n}",
